{le} will give you something specific that you have in mind but will not
specify that it is aforementioned. The English definite article will. For
example, "A dog bit the boy. The dog went into the house" refers to one dog
across both sentences. {lo gerku cu batci lo nanla .i le gerku cu klama lo
zdani} does not do this; the dog in the second sentence is specific but
could be an entirely new dog. {lo bi'u nai gerku} would not have had this
problem.

-mi'e la latro'a mu'o

